// Zealan god animation — the one-shot shatter-and-wake driver.
//
// WHY THIS CLASS IS PINNED TO 860 AND CANNOT MOVE. The engine picks the
// usecode class for an item's events from its SHAPE NUMBER:
//
//     uint32 class_id = _shape;          // item.cpp:1516
//
// so shape 860's anim() event lands in class 860, and nowhere else. This is
// not a manifest preference; renumbering it silently stops the gods moving.
// `lv_manifest.json` pins TYPEZEALANGOD to 860 for that reason.
//
// The event is delivered because shape 860's TYPEFLAG entry carries
// animType 5 ("call the item's usecode anim()"), written by
// lv_god_statues.py through patch_typeflag.set_anim. The engine then runs
//
//     if (animType && (gametick % animSpeed) == 0) animateItem();
//
// every time the item is drawn (item.cpp:1778), and animateItem's case 5 is
// a bare callUsecodeEvent_anim(). animSpeed is 1, so this handler is called
// on every tick the god is inside the fast area.
//
// Seven retail shapes use the same mechanism and every one has a class at
// its own shape number: HOURGLAS 227, DRIPS 348, FIREITEM 397, FIREFELD 400,
// CLRLAVA 409, BUBLAST 483, DRIPS2 653. DRIPS is the five-line reference
// implementation this is modelled on — increment the frame, wrap, fire a
// sound on one particular frame, setFrame.
//
// FRAME LAYOUT (shape 860, 42 frames). 0-5 are exactly where they have
// always been, because build_map_18.py places frames 0/1/2 and
// test_sanctum_clearance.py asserts them:
//
//     0,1,2    encased  Felicitar, Doloras, Timyra   REST
//     3,4,5    freed    Felicitar, Doloras, Timyra   REST
//     6..17    Felicitar's run   (6 shatter, 6 wake)
//     18..29   Doloras's run
//     30..41   Timyra's run
//
// so a god's run starts at 6 + encasedFrame * 12 and ends 11 frames later on
// the freed rest frame. Two rest bands, one run per god, and the encased
// frame doubles as the god's identity — no quality lookup needed.
//
// THE GATE IS THE WHOLE DESIGN. anim() fires for every shape-860 item in the
// fast area, which includes all three gods the moment the player walks into
// the sanctum, years before the ceremony. Frames under 6 return immediately,
// so a sealed god sits still until AOSCENE kicks her with setFrame().

uses "item";

typeclass TypeZealanGod inherits Item
{
	process anim();
}

process TypeZealanGod::anim()
{
	f:Number = 0;

	f = getFrame();

	// REST. Frames 0-5 are the two static states — encased and freed — and
	// neither advances on its own. Everything the player sees before the
	// ceremony, and everything they see after they walk away and come back,
	// lands here.
	if f < 6
	{
		return;
	}

	// END OF A RUN. Each god's 12 frames finish on her freed rest frame, so
	// the animation stops itself and the result is a state FIXED.DAT and
	// EggTempleEntry already know how to restore.
	if f = 17
	{
		setFrame(3);
		return;
	}
	if f = 29
	{
		setFrame(4);
		return;
	}
	if f = 41
	{
		setFrame(5);
		return;
	}

	setFrame(f + 1);
}
